yaml/scalar
description: Atomic token - a string, a number, a boolean, a null, or an alias
- >
  An atomic token. An UNQUOTED one resolves its type from its content - the null and boolean
  literals, the number shapes, everything else a string - while quoting or a block header
  always makes a string. See the subchapters below for the types, each with its own concretes:
- !!<format: text/x-yaml> |
  a: plain text
  b: 'single quoted'
  c: 42
  d: true
  e: ~
- *: 00-yaml_string
- *: 01-yaml_number
- *: 02-yaml_boolean
- *: 03-yaml_null
- *: 04-yaml_alias
